md("# 04 — Explanation and advice · Crowdfund Compass (Group 11)\nGoal: turn the final model into things a coach or founder can use: why a campaign scores as it does, six area scores, the single changes that are associated with better odds, and a verdict.\n\nWorkflow: 1) Setup → 2) Load model and data → 3) SHAP → 4) Area scores → 5) Chance range and verdict rule → 6) What to change → 7) Product types that do badly → 8) Explanation tree → 9) Examples → 10) Conclusions.\n\n**Read this first:** everything here describes associations in past campaigns. A suggested change is \"campaigns that did this were funded more often\", never a promise.\n\nRun notebook 03 first (it saves the model). *AI use: code written with Claude (Fable 5.2), 16.11.2026; reviewed by the team.*")
md("## 1) Setup")
code("import sys, time, json, warnings, os\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n!pip -q install vaderSentiment\nimport numpy as np, pandas as pd, joblib, xgboost as xgb\nfrom sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier, export_text\nfrom sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\npd.set_option('display.width', 250); pd.set_option('display.max_rows', 200); pd.set_option('display.max_colwidth', 90)\n\n# from google.colab import drive; drive.mount('/content/drive')\nproject = 'drive/My Drive/crowdfund_compass'      # folder with features.py, modeling.py, advice.py\nout = project + '/models'                         # written by notebook 03\nsys.path.insert(0, project)\nimport features as F, modeling as M, advice as A")
md("## 2) Load the model and the data\nTraining campaigns (2023–24) are the reference population; the 2025 test year is used to check everything.")
code(ch[0])
md("## 3) SHAP: what drives the score? (beyond class)\n*Why:* a coach needs reasons, not only a number. *In plain words:* SHAP splits each campaign's score into one piece per feature: how much that feature pushed the score up or down compared with an average campaign. The pieces add up exactly to the model's score (checked below).")
code(ch[1])
md("**Interpretation:** what the product is (Market) and who launches it (Founder) account for more than half of the explanation. The areas a founder can change before launch (Ambition, Presentation, Timing, Pitch) account for the rest.")
md("## 4) Area scores, 0–100\nFor each of the six areas we add up the SHAP pieces of its features and ask: what share of the reference campaigns had a lower sum? 50 = typical, 100 = this area helps more than in every reference campaign. Bands: 0–25 weak (red), 26–60 to improve (amber), 61–100 strong (green). The check below shows that campaigns with a weak area were funded less often in 2025.")
code(ch[2])
md("## 5) Chance range and the verdict rule\n- **High end** of the range: calibrated chance in our sample. **Low end:** the same after the shift to Kickstarter's official rates.\n- The ranking of campaigns is solid, the levels are rough. So **Rethink** is decided by rank: the riskiest share of the cohort that the coach has capacity for (default 30%), ranked by the low end.\n- To see what that means outside our sample, the 2025 test year is re-weighted so that each parent category has Kickstarter's official share of failures.")
code(ch[3])
md("## 6) What to change\nFor each campaign the module tries one change at a time on the levers a founder controls (goal in steps down to the minimum budget, duration, launch day, video, pre-launch page, more preparation time, title and blurb length) and keeps the best option per lever. Here on 4,000 campaigns of 2025, with the minimum budget assumed at half the goal.")
code(ch[4])
md("**Interpretation:** for more than four in ten campaigns no single change adds 2 points. The largest associations are with a pre-launch page and more preparation time. Both stand for groundwork (building an audience before launch): opening a page the day before launch will not add these points.")
md("## 7) Product types that do badly\nThe Market score mostly reflects what is being made. A very low score is a signal for the coach that the product type itself has rarely been funded on Kickstarter.")
code(ch[5])
md("## 8) Explanation tree (class: decision tree)\nA depth-3 tree on features a founder can read (no text score, no category codes). The app shows the campaign's path through it.")
code(tree)
md("## 9) Three example campaigns from 2025")
code(ch[7])
md("### Cohort check\nSimulated cohorts of 40 campaigns drawn from 2025; the coach takes the 12 riskiest.")
code(coh)
md("## 10) Save")
code(ch[8])
md("## Conclusions\n1. Market and Founder explain more than half of the score; the levers a founder controls explain the rest.\n2. Area scores separate campaigns well: weak areas go with clearly lower funded rates.\n3. Verdict: Rethink = riskiest share of the cohort by rank (default 30%); Adjust = one change adds at least 5 points; Launch = otherwise.\n4. In a cohort with Kickstarter's official mix, the riskiest 30% contain about half of all failures, and nearly all of them fail.\n5. Advice is association, not cause.")
